<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm12-wenchang ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 12 / SatNet LEO group (Hainan Commercial LC-2, Wenchang) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 15.00 s, kick 0.750 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 8320 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.3904-0.000811*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 12 (CZ-12, CALT) (sim/vehicles/lm12.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-12: thrust/Isp from huijiwiki (YF-100K SL pair, YF-115B thrust) + Wikipedia (YF-115 Isp, GLOW); stage masses DERIVED from published burn times with an ASSUMED 0.92 structure coefficient; event times = CALT TYPICAL Y7 sequence (huijiwiki), not this flight&#x27;s.
T0 = LL2 NET 2026-11-08T20:25:00Z (Sun 8 Nov 12:25 pm PST; window 20:17-20:47Z), delayed per NOTAMs. Payload: SatNet LEO group, 9 satellites (LL2). Event times = CALT TYPICAL LM-12 Y7 sequence (huijiwiki), not this flight&#x27;s. UNTUNED: no altitude/range knots exist to tune against.
Target (see launch config): insertion 300 km, apoapsis 300 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 109.33 deg; payload 8320 kg.
Pad: 19.597550N 110.936481E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-08T20:25:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+622.5 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+1731 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF burn &#x27;S2 restart (2x YF-115B)&#x27;: ign T+1622.5 s, 18.0 s at 360.00 kN prograde (Isp 341.5 s); published TYPICAL timing and full published thrust, flown open-loop prograde; purpose (orbit raise vs. other) and this flight&#x27;s actual restart timing unpublished, so the resulting orbit is ILLUSTRATIVE only
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+1731 s (CALT typical LM-12 Y7 sequence via huijiwiki: first satellite batch separation T+1730.505 s (TYPICAL, not flight-specific)): alt 305.25 km, osculating 294.3 x 2275.8 km, i 36.844 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Second satellite batch separation 1780.505 s in the typical sequence is not drawn separately (50 s later on the same coast).</description>
